 {
  "coord": "12:5",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "term",
  "note": "'Apprehend' means 'think of', not 'fear'; 'Fear nothing but fun' garbles the meaning.",
  "replacement": "FLORIZEL. Think of nothing but fun. The gods themselves, lowering their divinity for love, have taken the shapes of beasts. Jupiter became a bull and bellowed. Green Neptune became a ram and bleated. And the fire-robed god, golden Apollo, became a poor humble swain, as I seem now. Their transformations were never for a piece of beauty rarer, nor in a way so chaste, since my desires don't run ahead of my honor, nor do my lusts burn hotter than my faith."
 },
